+    # Verify every requested element independently of the solver's own
+    # convergence test, so a reported success cannot retain a large
+    # trace-element residual.
+    #
+    # The test compares the request of this level, x_req (molfracs_atoms
+    # passed to the solve, before this level's rainout), with the returned
+    # TOTAL elemental inventory x_tot = molfracs_atoms, the atoms of the gas
+    # plus the condensed phases of the returned state, both normalized to unit
+    # sum:  max_e |x_tot,e / x_req,e - 1| <= closure_rtol over the elements
+    # with x_req,e > 0.  It applies with and without a condensed phase.  The
+    # gas vector molfracs_atoms_gas is not compared: it is renormalized over
+    # the gas alone, so it differs from the request by the condensed fraction
+    # by construction; with rainout it becomes the next level's request.
+    # Equilibrate returns zero for every condensate outside the final
+    # included set of the solve, so a condensed amount carried over from the
+    # previous level by use_prev_guess is not part of x_tot.
+    closure_rtol = max(1.0e-8, 100.0*gas.mass_tol)
+
+    # Compute chemical equilibrium at all altitudes.
+    try:
+        for i in range(P.shape[0]):
+            gas.use_prev_guess = i > 0
+            accepted = False
